    "body": "Migrating a legacy wallet that holds no spendable material fails whenever the\nwallet contains transactions. `migratewallet` returns\n`std::bad_function_call (-1)` and the wallet is left unmigrated.\n\nTwo defects are involved, and the first one hides the second.\n\n### 1. The migration check reads in-memory state that has not been updated yet\n\nWhen the wallet being migrated has no spendable material,\n`CWallet::ApplyMigrationData()` asserts that nothing is left behind in it:\n\n```cpp\nif (!m_address_book.empty()) return util::Error{_(\"Error: Not all address book records were migrated\")};\nif (!mapWallet.empty()) return util::Error{_(\"Error: Not all transaction records were migrated\")};\n```\n\nThe two checks look symmetric but are not. `DelAddressBookWithDB()` erases from\n`m_address_book` straight away, so the first check sees current state.\n`RemoveTxs()` only erases the transaction records from disk; it defers the\n`mapWallet` removal to the db txn's `on_commit` listener, which does not run\nuntil the txn is committed — after `ApplyMigrationData()` has returned.\n\n`mapWallet` is therefore never empty at that point and the check always fails.\n\n### 2. Aborting the txn calls a callback that was never set\n\n`DbTxnListener` declares `on_commit` and `on_abort` as plain `std::function`\nmembers and callers may set only the one they need. `RemoveTxs()` does exactly\nthat: `on_commit` is set, `on_abort` is left empty.\n\n`TxnCommit()` and `TxnAbort()` each invoked their listener's callback\nunconditionally, so the abort triggered by the failed check above threw\n`std::bad_function_call`. The exception escaped the wallet entirely, replacing\nthe real error with an unhelpful one and skipping the caller's cleanup path.\n\n### Fix\n\nThe first commit skips callbacks that are not set, and documents that they are\noptional. The second discounts the transactions already queued for deletion\ninstead of requiring `mapWallet` to be empty.\n\nThey are kept separate because the second defect masks the first: with only the\nlistener fix applied, the migration surfaces the real error\n`Error: Not all transaction records were migrated (-4)` instead of\n`std::bad_function_call (-1)`.\n\n### Testing\n\n`src/wallet/test/db_tests.cpp` gains a regression test covering a listener with\nonly one callback set, for both commit and abort. It fails on master with\n`std::bad_function_call` and passes with the fix.\n\n`test/functional/wallet_migration.py` gains a case migrating a blank legacy\nwallet with a watch-only address that has received a transaction. The test is\ntaken from #36483.\n\nTo reproduce on master, apply the functional test alone and run\n`wallet_migration.py`.\n\nFixes #36483",
