        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet: skip unset db txn listener callbacks\n\nDbTxnListener declares on_commit and on_abort as plain std::function\nmembers and callers may set only the one they need. RemoveTxs() does\nexactly that: it registers a listener with on_commit set and on_abort\nleft empty.\n\nTxnCommit() and TxnAbort() invoked both unconditionally, so aborting a\ndb txn in which RemoveTxs() had run threw std::bad_function_call. The\nexception escaped the wallet, replacing the error that caused the abort\nwith an unhelpful \"std::bad_function_call\" RPC error and skipping the\ncaller's cleanup path.\n\nSkip callbacks that are not set, and document that they are optional.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "yusufyildiz34",
        "email": "yusufyildiz86@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-20T11:32:00Z"
      },
